# Ignore Obsidian workspace configuration
.obsidian/

# Obsidian stub notes. The repo root is an Obsidian vault, and blog posts link to
# site routes as root-relative markdown (`](/blog/how-to-make-a-discord-form)`).
# Obsidian reads those as vault paths and creates an empty .md at that path the
# moment one is clicked — so `/blog/`, `/use-cases/`, `/tutorials/` and root-level
# `foo.md` appear out of nowhere. Real content is under src/, docs/ and public/;
# the only tracked .md files at the root are the two below.
/*.md
!/README.md
!/CLAUDE.md
/blog/
/use-cases/
/tutorials/
